gmeow:payloadSchemaYamlLdArchive
    a gmeow:PayloadSchema ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "payload schema — YAML-LD archive"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The CLAIM CORPUS's JSON-LD-star and YAML-LD-star projections: the RDF 1.2 statement layer rendered into the JSON-LD family, tarred by gmeow:stage-archive-blobs off gmeow:stage-statements' rendered surface so a JSON-LD-family consumer reads the reified statement layer straight out of the bundle. NOT the whole carrier — that document is the make build deliverable dist/gmeow.jsonld, which rides no frame. Its members carry no committed generated/ path, so it appears in no gmeow:FanoutExtraction row: the archive is a bundle-only deliverable, not a reconstruction target. It carries NO gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary. A claim dictionary once primed it together with gmeow:payloadSchemaStatementsArchive, on the reasoning that this frame alone — roughly nine kilobytes — is too small a population for any cell of the (strategy × target-length) grid to pay for. Measured over the whole two-frame claim corpus it still did not pay: the frames coded 2,635 B smaller while the dictionary's own in-band bytes cost 4,094 B, so it was retired rather than shipped as dead weight."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:payloadSchemaId "yaml-ld-archive" ;
    gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxConfigBox .

# --- Named failure classes -------------------------------------------------- #
# Each is a HARD FAIL. None of them ever authorizes a fallback to dictionary-less
# decode: a payload written through a primed medium is not readable at lower
# fidelity without its dictionary, it is not readable AT ALL, so "retry without
# the dictionary" would produce garbage that passes as content. They are wired
# from gmeow:MediumEnvelope through gmeow:enforcesFailureClass, and the opacity
# case reuses the existing gmeow:OpaqueFrame / gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec
# vocabulary rather than modelling a disjoint set — a medium a reader cannot
# apply is exactly the vantage-relative opacity the transport module already
# describes.

gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS Conformance Failure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The parent of the GTS transport well-formedness failure vocabulary: a violation is itself a typed, queryable object, and each slice logic:Constraint points at its failure class through gmeow:enforcesFailureClass. Conformance here enforces WELL-FORMEDNESS of the transport claims — that a declared dictionary resolves, that a payload rep is registered, that a digest matches — never the truth of the content the transport carries."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this class roots the TRANSPORT well-formedness failure vocabulary and nothing else. It does not cover a content claim being false, a validation report or finding record, or the gate that raises a failure — a logic:Constraint points at its failure class through gmeow:enforcesFailureClass, and the class stays the name of the violation rather than the name of the check."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for a CONTENT claim being false (transport conformance is about bytes, order, and resolvability) and avoid minting a failure subclass with no constraint that raises it — an unenforced failure class is documentation, not a gate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Subclass it for each named transport failure and point the raising logic:Constraint at the subclass with gmeow:enforcesFailureClass, so a query moves from gate to failure and back."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the root of the gts slice's typed conformance-failure vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:GtsFrameProfileViolation
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS Frame Profile Violation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when authored GTS bytes do not carry the ONE mandated frame profile: a payload-bearing frame whose transform chain is not zstd-rsyncable, a codec catalog entry that declares no level or a level other than the mandated one, a torn CBOR sequence, or bytes that do not begin with a segment header. HARD FAIL: the transform contract is a distribution invariant, not a preference — a consumer resolves a frame by the catalog the header declares, so a frame outside the profile is not a weaker bundle but an undecodable one. It is raised both by the single production emitter, which refuses to author such bytes, and by the wire-level audit that re-reads them."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:bundleWithGzipFrame a gmeow:GtsFrameProfileViolation ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure names a violation of the FRAME AUTHORSHIP profile — the transform, its declared level, and the wire framing that carries them. It is not a dictionary resolution failure (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary), not a digest disagreement (gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch), and not a judgment on the RDF the frames carry: the payload may be perfectly well-formed inside a frame nothing can decode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid resolving it by widening the accepted transform set or by lowering the declared level to match the bytes — the profile is the contract the bytes must meet, not a description of them. Avoid using it for a frame whose transform is correct but whose declared dictionary does not resolve; that is gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by the mandated authorship emitter and by the wire-level frame audit that proves any producer's output; resolve it by re-authoring the bytes through the one production entry, never by relaxing the audit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name GTS bytes that fall outside the mandated one-transform frame profile."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumCorpusDrift
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Corpus Drift"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when the corpus identity a dictionary's evidence records is not the identity of the corpus at hand — the committed sweep table (bench/medium-baseline.json) naming a gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest this build did not resolve, or two gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization records of one dictionary disagreeing about which corpus produced it. It exists because a gmeow:DictionaryCorpus is a SELECTOR re-resolved on every build: an archive that gains or loses one member moves the corpus while the committed evidence sits still, and every verdict read out of that evidence — the winner-table bijection, the declared-is-argmin agreement, the pays-for-itself criterion — would then be about a sweep nobody re-ran. HARD FAIL: stale evidence is not weaker evidence, it is evidence about a different corpus, so a build refuses rather than grading itself against it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:realCoreV1 a gmeow:MediumCorpusDrift ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a mismatch of CORPUS IDENTITY between recorded evidence and the corpus this build resolved. It is not a mismatch between a dictionary's recorded digest and its own bytes (that is gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch), not a dropped dictionary version (gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression), and not a verdict on the dictionary: the shipped bytes may be perfectly good while the numbers describing them are about different material."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid resolving it by editing the recorded digest (that asserts an identity nothing measured — re-run the sweep instead), avoid downgrading it to a warning, and avoid using it for a dictionary whose BYTES do not match their digest — that is gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by logic:MediumCorpusIdentityAgreementConstraint and by the build's own re-derivation of every resolved corpus's digest; resolve it by re-running `make maint-medium-sweep` over the moved corpus, never by relaxing the comparison."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name evidence about a dictionary that describes a corpus other than the one the build resolved."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Dictionary Regression"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when an EMITTED dictionary version is no longer retained by any authored gmeow:CompressionDictionary — a gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization whose gmeow:dictionaryVersion its gmeow:realizesDictionary definition does not declare. HARD FAIL: every artifact already primed with that version becomes undecodable the moment the version is dropped, so retiring a version is a data-destroying change, not a cleanup. There is no fallback to dictionary-less decode — a frame primed with version N cannot be read without version N."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:realCoreV0 a gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a REGRESSION in what the bundle's dictionaries deliver — an emitted version no authored definition still declares, or a shipped dictionary whose two-part code stops beating its no-dictionary baseline. It is not an unresolvable dictionary reference (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary), not a byte-identity disagreement (gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch), and not a tidiness warning: what it names is artifacts that have become unreadable, or bytes consumers pay for and do not get back."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating it as a warning about tidiness (it names artifacts that have become unreadable) and avoid resolving it by deleting the realization — the shipped bytes it describes still exist."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by logic:MediumDictionaryRetentionConstraint; resolve it by restoring the dropped gmeow:dictionaryVersion to its authored definition, never by suppressing the check."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the loss of a dictionary version that shipped artifacts still depend on."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Digest Mismatch"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a digest a medium envelope carries does not match the bytes it describes — the frame's gmeow:contentDigest against the payload, the gmeow:strataDigest against its named gmeow:envelopeDigestStratum, or a dictionary's gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest against the dictionary the reader holds. HARD FAIL and never a fallback: decoding a primed payload against a DIFFERENT dictionary with the same id produces plausible-looking garbage rather than an error, so a digest mismatch must refuse before any decode is attempted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:env a gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a disagreement between a DIGEST an envelope carries and the BYTES at hand — payload against gmeow:contentDigest, stratum against gmeow:strataDigest, or the held dictionary against gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest. It is not a missing declaration (gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary) and not an unresolvable one (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary): here the reference resolves and the bytes behind it are the wrong ones."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid downgrading it to a warning and avoid retrying the decode with a different dictionary — a mismatch means the reader's premises are wrong, not that it should search."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raise it before priming whenever a carried digest disagrees with the bytes at hand; pair it with the frame's gmeow:OpaqueFrame record when the region is surfaced rather than rejected wholesale."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a byte-identity disagreement between a medium envelope's claims and the bytes it describes."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Opaque Frame"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a reader lacks a capability the frame's medium declares through gmeow:requiresReaderCapability — rsyncable framing or dictionary priming (GTS spec §8.4 makes both non-baseline). It is DELIBERATELY not a disjoint new opacity model: the reader surfaces the region through the existing gmeow:OpaqueFrame vocabulary with gmeow:opacityReason gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec, and this class names the medium-axis reading of that same situation. HARD FAIL for a producer (emitting through a medium whose capabilities the target reader lacks is a mis-declared deliverable) and a surfaced, describable gap for a reader — never a silent dictionary-less decode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:frame7 a gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame ; gmeow:opacityReason gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a READER-SIDE capability gap: the frame is well formed and its declarations resolve, but the reader cannot do what gmeow:requiresReaderCapability demands. It is not a defect in the frame, not a missing dictionary declaration (gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary), and not a dictionary the reader could name but not resolve (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary). It is also not a new opacity model — the region is surfaced through the existing gmeow:OpaqueFrame vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid modelling it as a new opacity axis (reuse gmeow:OpaqueFrame / gmeow:opacityReason) and avoid using it where the reader HAS the capability but the dictionary is missing — that is gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Surface the region as a gmeow:OpaqueFrame carrying gmeow:opacityUnknownCodec and type it with this class so the medium-axis cause is queryable; compare the reader's capabilities against gmeow:requiresReaderCapability to report exactly which one is missing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a frame a reader cannot decode because it lacks a capability the medium declares."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Undeclared Dictionary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a gmeow:MediumEnvelope does not declare its contract — canonically a payload primed with a dictionary whose frame declares none, and equally any of the six unconditionally exactly-one envelope fields being absent or duplicated, or a missing gmeow:envelopeDictionary on an envelope whose medium declares one, since a projection missing a coordinate is a different claim rather than a weaker one. It is ALSO the failure of a registered gmeow:PayloadSchema carrying no gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium: the rep-to-medium assignment is total, so a missing row is a missing DECLARATION rather than permission to encode the rep unmediated. HARD FAIL: an undeclared dictionary is undiscoverable, so the payload is permanently undecodable even though its bytes are intact. It is distinct from gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary (a dictionary IS declared but does not resolve): here nothing was declared at all, and there is no fallback to dictionary-less decode because the bytes were not written that way. This is the failure the DERIVED gmeow:MediumEnvelope contract shape raises, which is why it is the class wired directly from gmeow:MediumEnvelope."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:env a gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a MISSING or DUPLICATED declaration — an envelope field of the seven-field contract absent or repeated, or a registered schema carrying no medium assignment. It is not a declaration that fails to resolve (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary) and not an unregistered payload rep (gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema): nothing was written down at all, so there is nothing to look up. Declaring no dictionary under the dictionary-less baseline medium is a SELECTION and stays outside this failure."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for the explicitly dictionary-less gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 (declaring no dictionary is that medium's SELECTION, not an omission) and avoid confusing it with an unresolvable declaration."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by the derived gmeow:MediumEnvelope contract shape whenever a field of the seven-field contract is absent or duplicated; the fix is to emit the declaration, never to decode without it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a primed payload whose priming dictionary was never written down."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:GtsDocumentSegmentedConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:GTSDocument carries at least one gmeow:gtsSegment. A document IS its ordered segment list — the composite identity is the heads taken in index order — so a document declaring no segment has no content to read and no identity to verify. A reader handed one cannot distinguish it from a file it failed to open, which is why the refusal happens here rather than being reported as an empty result."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:BundleArtifactUnreadable ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:GTSDocument ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "Every gmeow:GTSDocument must carry at least one gmeow:gtsSegment; a document with none has no content to read and no identity to verify (gmeow:BundleArtifactUnreadable)." ;
    logic:integrity gmeow:gdsForall .
gmeow:gdsForall a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented constraint formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top-level forall-implies-exists integrity formula of gmeow:GtsDocumentSegmentedConstraint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall gmeow:gdsImpl .
gmeow:gdsImpl a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented implication"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The implication of the GTS document segmented constraint: every gmeow:GTSDocument (the antecedent gmeow:gdsGuard) satisfies the existential consequent gmeow:gdsCons."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:antecedent gmeow:gdsGuard ; logic:consequent gmeow:gdsCons .
gmeow:gdsGuard a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented antecedent type guard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The antecedent of gmeow:gdsImpl: the guarded subject is a gmeow:GTSDocument. It selects what the constraint ranges over, so a subject outside this class discharges the implication vacuously rather than violating it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:GTSDocument ] .
gmeow:gdsCons a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented existential consequent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The consequent of gmeow:gdsImpl: there EXISTS a value v satisfying gmeow:gdsAtom. The quantifier is what makes the constraint a cardinality claim rather than a claim about one named value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:exists gmeow:gdsAtom .
gmeow:gdsAtom a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS document segmented relational atom"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The atom under gmeow:gdsCons's existential: the guarded subject stands in gmeow:gtsSegment to the quantified value v."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation gmeow:gtsSegment ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .

gmeow:GtsSegmentHeadedConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:GTSSegment carries its gmeow:gtsHeadId. The head is a BLAKE3 content-id committing transitively to the segment's whole frame history, so it is what makes the bytes CHECKABLE — a segment without one can be parsed into terms but never verified against the chain it claims to continue, and a reader has no way to tell a good read from a corrupted one."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:BundleSourceUnparsable ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:GTSSegment ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "Every gmeow:GTSSegment must carry a gmeow:gtsHeadId; a segment with no head can be parsed but never verified against the chain it claims to continue (gmeow:BundleSourceUnparsable)." ;
    logic:integrity gmeow:gshForall .
gmeow:gshForall a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed constraint formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top-level forall-implies-exists integrity formula of gmeow:GtsSegmentHeadedConstraint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall gmeow:gshImpl .
gmeow:gshImpl a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed implication"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The implication of the GTS segment headed constraint: every gmeow:GTSSegment (the antecedent gmeow:gshGuard) satisfies the existential consequent gmeow:gshCons."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:antecedent gmeow:gshGuard ; logic:consequent gmeow:gshCons .
gmeow:gshGuard a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed antecedent type guard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The antecedent of gmeow:gshImpl: the guarded subject is a gmeow:GTSSegment. It selects what the constraint ranges over, so a subject outside this class discharges the implication vacuously rather than violating it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:GTSSegment ] .
gmeow:gshCons a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed existential consequent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The consequent of gmeow:gshImpl: there EXISTS a value v satisfying gmeow:gshAtom. The quantifier is what makes the constraint a cardinality claim rather than a claim about one named value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:exists gmeow:gshAtom .
gmeow:gshAtom a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment headed relational atom"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The atom under gmeow:gshCons's existential: the guarded subject stands in gmeow:gtsHeadId to the quantified value v."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation gmeow:gtsHeadId ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .

gmeow:GtsSegmentProfiledConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:GTSSegment declares its gmeow:gtsProfile. The profile states what the segment is FOR, and a flat projection reads it to decide which of the segment's claims a lossy surface may carry — CSVW, SKOS, OBO Graphs and the rest each drop what they cannot encode. A segment with no declared profile leaves the projector guessing, and a projector that guesses publishes a smaller ontology under the same name rather than refusing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:FlatExportRefused ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:GTSSegment ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "Every gmeow:GTSSegment must declare a gmeow:gtsProfile; a projector reading an undeclared segment guesses what it may drop (gmeow:FlatExportRefused)." ;
    logic:integrity gmeow:gspForall .
gmeow:gspForall a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled constraint formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top-level forall-implies-exists integrity formula of gmeow:GtsSegmentProfiledConstraint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall gmeow:gspImpl .
gmeow:gspImpl a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled implication"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The implication of the GTS segment profiled constraint: every gmeow:GTSSegment (the antecedent gmeow:gspGuard) satisfies the existential consequent gmeow:gspCons."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:antecedent gmeow:gspGuard ; logic:consequent gmeow:gspCons .
gmeow:gspGuard a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled antecedent type guard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The antecedent of gmeow:gspImpl: the guarded subject is a gmeow:GTSSegment. It selects what the constraint ranges over, so a subject outside this class discharges the implication vacuously rather than violating it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:GTSSegment ] .
gmeow:gspCons a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled existential consequent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The consequent of gmeow:gspImpl: there EXISTS a value v satisfying gmeow:gspAtom. The quantifier is what makes the constraint a cardinality claim rather than a claim about one named value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:exists gmeow:gspAtom .
gmeow:gspAtom a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "GTS segment profiled relational atom"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The atom under gmeow:gspCons's existential: the guarded subject stands in gmeow:gtsProfile to the quantified value v."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation gmeow:gtsProfile ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .

gmeow:CompressionDictionaryIdentifiedConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Compression dictionary identified constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:CompressionDictionary declares the gmeow:dictionaryId it is pinned under. The id is the ONLY key a consumer has: a runtime store resolves its priming bytes by looking that string up in the shipped bundle's in-band header map, so a dictionary declared without one can be trained, shipped and still be unreachable — the store asks for a name the bundle never wrote down, and there is no weaker unprimed store to fall back to because the store's own header is what makes it decodable. This is the authoring-side cause of the consumer engine's refusal, caught where the dictionary is declared rather than where it is opened. Measured to hold over all six shipped dictionaries, so the record is a live gate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnpinnedStoreDictionary ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CompressionDictionary ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "Every gmeow:CompressionDictionary must declare a gmeow:dictionaryId; a dictionary with no id cannot be resolved out of the shipped bundle's in-band map (gmeow:MediumUnpinnedStoreDictionary)." ;
    logic:integrity gmeow:cdiForall .
gmeow:cdiForall a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "compression-dictionary-identified formula"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The top-level forall-implies-exists integrity formula of gmeow:CompressionDictionaryIdentifiedConstraint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall gmeow:cdiImpl .
gmeow:cdiImpl a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "compression-dictionary-identified implication"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The implication of the compression-dictionary-identified constraint: every gmeow:CompressionDictionary (the antecedent gmeow:cdiGuard) satisfies the existential consequent gmeow:cdiCons."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:antecedent gmeow:cdiGuard ; logic:consequent gmeow:cdiCons .
gmeow:cdiGuard a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "compression-dictionary-identified antecedent type guard"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The antecedent of gmeow:cdiImpl: the guarded subject is a gmeow:CompressionDictionary. It selects what the constraint ranges over, so a subject outside this class discharges the implication vacuously rather than violating it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] .
gmeow:cdiCons a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "compression-dictionary-identified existential consequent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The consequent of gmeow:cdiImpl: there EXISTS a value v satisfying gmeow:cdiAtom. The quantifier is what makes the constraint a cardinality claim rather than a claim about one named value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:exists gmeow:cdiAtom .
gmeow:cdiAtom a logic:Formula ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "compression-dictionary-identified relational atom"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The atom under gmeow:cdiCons's existential: the guarded subject stands in gmeow:dictionaryId to the quantified value v."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ; logic:relation gmeow:dictionaryId ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .

gmeow:BundleArtifactUnreadable
    a owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Bundle Artifact Unreadable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a read-side consumer cannot READ a source artifact at all — a Turtle source handed to the native query substrate, or a materialized gmeow.gts. It is a byte-level refusal below any RDF judgment: nothing was parsed, so nothing can be said about what the artifact contains. HARD FAIL rather than an empty dataset, because an empty result is indistinguishable from an artifact that legitimately carries nothing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:BundleSourceUnparsable
    a owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Bundle Source Unparsable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised on the READ side when bytes were obtained but are not the RDF the reader requires: a syntactically invalid Turtle source, a query evaluation failure, or a query whose result form is not the one the caller demands. Distinct from gmeow:BundleArtifactUnreadable, where the bytes never arrived: here they did and are wrong, so the reader refuses rather than returning a partial binding set that would read as a complete answer over less data."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:FlatExportRefused
    a owl:Class ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Flat Export Refused"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a flat-export projection — CSVW, SKOS, OBO Graphs, N-Quads, TriG — cannot carry a term the bundle holds, or is asked for a configuration it refuses. The projection is REFUSED rather than degraded: a flat surface that silently drops a term it cannot encode publishes a smaller ontology under the same name, and a consumer has no way to learn what is missing. Every declared loss belongs in the distribution catalog, where it is queryable, never in a projection that quietly omits."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:MediumUnpinnedStoreDictionary
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Unpinned Store Dictionary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a CONSUMER's runtime store — agent memory, the conjecture library, the candidate library — must be primed with a shipped dictionary the loaded gmeow.gts pins no in-band bytes for. The bundle is the dictionary's distribution channel: it pins every declared dictionary in its segment header precisely so a consumer writes the exact bytes the build trained, never a re-derivation that could differ under the same id and never an out-of-band artifact a wheel-mode install would not have. HARD FAIL: there is no weaker unprimed store to fall back to, because the store's OWN header is what makes it decodable, and writing it unprimed would silently discard the density the dictionary exists to provide. It is a READ-SIDE failure of the shipped artifact, which is what distinguishes it from gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary (an authoring-side omission — a rep or envelope that never wrote its contract down) and from gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary (a declaration that resolves to no registered gmeow:CompressionDictionary): here the declaration is fine and the BUNDLE is short."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:store a gmeow:MediumUnpinnedStoreDictionary ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: the consumer engine's store lane alone. The producer is the engine that opens the store (crates/mcp), never the build — the pipeline's own rep-to-medium checks raise gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary, and one failure class carries exactly one producer so 'which code raised this' always has an answer."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for an authoring omission (gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary), for a declaration that fails to resolve (gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary), or for the dictionary-less baseline medium, where naming no dictionary IS the selection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by the consumer engine when it resolves a store's medium out of the loaded bundle's in-band \"dct\" map and the id is absent; the fix is to regenerate the bundle so it ships the dictionary, never to open the store unprimed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a runtime store that cannot be primed because the shipped bundle does not carry the dictionary it names."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Unknown Dictionary"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a frame declares a dictionary that does not resolve to a registered gmeow:CompressionDictionary — an unknown id, an unknown version, or a dictionary the reader does not hold. HARD FAIL: there is NO fallback to dictionary-less decode, because zstd priming changes the code, not the framing — decoding without the dictionary the encoder used yields corrupt output that no checksum in the payload itself would catch."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:env a gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers a declaration that RESOLVES TO NOTHING — an unknown dictionary id or version, or one the reader does not hold. It is not an absent declaration (gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary), not a resolved dictionary whose bytes disagree with their digest (gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch), and not a reader that lacks dictionary support at all (gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid recovering from it by decoding unprimed (that produces garbage, not degraded content) and avoid using it for an undeclared dictionary — that is gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raised by logic:MediumDictionaryResolutionConstraint; a reader raises it before priming and refuses the frame, optionally surfacing it as a gmeow:OpaqueFrame so the gap is described rather than dropped."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a declared dictionary that cannot be resolved to registered bytes."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema
    a logic:Category ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "Medium Unknown Schema"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ;
    skos:definition "The failure raised when a blob's rep does not resolve to a registered gmeow:PayloadSchema. HARD FAIL, and the reason the registry exists at all: if the schema were merely derived from the frame, an unregistered rep would decode as an unclassified blob with an UNDEFINED medium assignment, which is exactly the silent capability degradation the no-optionality rule forbids. Adding an archive to the carrier without registering its schema raises this rather than shipping an unmediated payload."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:env a gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this failure covers an emitted payload REP that the closed gmeow:PayloadSchema registry does not know. It is not a missing medium assignment on a registered schema (that is gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary) and not a dictionary problem at all: the rep is unclassifiable, so no medium and no dictionary can even be looked up for it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:addedInVersion "0.1.0" ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid resolving it by inventing a default medium for the unknown rep (there is no defaultable answer) and avoid suppressing it while an archive ships unregistered."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernGTSPackaging ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Raise it whenever a rep label has no gmeow:payloadSchemaId match; the fix is to mint the schema individual in the same change that adds the archive."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:termStability gmeow:stabilityExperimental ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name an emitted payload representation that the schema registry does not know."@x-gmeow-english .

# gmeow:enforcesFailureClass is a GATE-to-failure link, and a class carries at most
# the ONE failure its own derived shape raises (the deriver hard-fails on distinct
# values for a shape target, exactly as gmeow:GmnEnvelope carries exactly one). So
# the envelope itself carries the failure of its own field-contract shape, and
# each of the other five is wired from the gate that actually raises it — the four
# range closures, the three procedural constraints, and the constraints below.
# Every one of them is reachable FROM gmeow:MediumEnvelope by following the gate's
# logic:formalizes edge back, so the whole named set stays anchored to the envelope
# without a class pretending to raise five different failures at once.
gmeow:MediumEnvelope gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary .

# A digest that is not a canonical 'blake3:<64 lowercase hex>' literal is
# indistinguishable from a truncated or foreign digest, so comparing it is a
# guaranteed mismatch rather than a check — the shape of the string is part of the
# claim, exactly as it is for gmeow:gtsHeadId.
logic:MediumStrataDigestFormConstraint
    a logic:StringPatternConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium strata-digest form constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:strataDigest is written 'blake3:<64 lowercase hex>'. A free-form digest cannot be compared against the bytes it claims to commit to, so a malformed one is a gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch by construction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:MediumEnvelope ;
    logic:valuePath gmeow:strataDigest ;
    logic:stringOp "regexRequired" ;
    logic:stringPattern "^blake3:[0-9a-f]{64}$" ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:MediumEnvelope ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:strataDigest must be written 'blake3:<64 lowercase hex>' — a free-form digest cannot be compared against the bytes it commits to." .

logic:MediumDictionaryDigestFormConstraint
    a logic:StringPatternConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium dictionary-digest form constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest is written 'blake3:<64 lowercase hex>'. A decoder compares this literal against the dictionary bytes it holds before priming, so a malformed value makes the comparison meaningless and the primed decode unsafe."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization ;
    logic:valuePath gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest ;
    logic:stringOp "regexRequired" ;
    logic:stringPattern "^blake3:[0-9a-f]{64}$" ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest must be written 'blake3:<64 lowercase hex>' — a decoder compares it against the dictionary it holds before priming." .

# A medium realized by a NON-BASELINE codec must declare the reader capability it
# demands. GTS spec §8.4 puts zstd-rsyncable outside the baseline reader contract,
# so an undeclared requirement means readers discover the gap only at decode time —
# which is exactly gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame, and exactly what Principle 13 forbids.
logic:MediumReaderCapabilityConstraint
    a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium reader-capability constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:Medium whose gmeow:mediumCodec is the non-baseline gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable names at least one gmeow:requiresReaderCapability. Raising the reader contract is a declared property of the deliverable (Principle 13), never a discovery a consumer makes mid-decode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ;
    logic:trigger gmeow:mediumCodec ;
    logic:triggerValue gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable ;
    logic:requires gmeow:requiresReaderCapability ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:Medium ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:Medium using the non-baseline gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable must declare at least one gmeow:requiresReaderCapability — an undeclared requirement surfaces as opacity at decode time." .

# The MANDATED FRAME PROFILE, stated as ontology rather than only as a wire audit.
#
# Every payload-bearing frame GMEOW authors carries one transform, gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable,
# at the declared level 12. The byte-level half of that rule is enforced by the authorship
# leaf, which refuses to emit non-conforming frames and re-reads them to prove it. This is
# its GRAPH half: a medium that declares the mandated level must also declare the mandated
# codec, so a medium claiming level-12 conformance while naming another codec is refused
# HERE, at authoring time, rather than only once bytes exist.
#
# Guarded on the CODEC and requiring the LEVEL. That is the direction the wire audit
# fails on: purrdf declares the level as a catalog parameter, so a catalog entry naming
# the mandated transform with NO declared level is unenforceable on the artifact — the
# audit cannot tell level 12 from level 3. Guarding the other way round (level implies
# codec) would also read on a literal trigger value, where every sibling guard in this
# slice triggers on an IRI.
logic:MediumMandatedFrameProfileConstraint
    a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium mandated frame-profile constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:Medium whose gmeow:mediumCodec is the mandated gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable must declare its gmeow:mediumZstdLevel. The mandated authorship profile is the PAIR (transform, level) — a medium naming the transform while leaving its level unstated claims conformance to a profile it does not pin, and the wire audit reading the emitted catalog cannot distinguish the mandated level from any other. HARD FAIL: the transform contract is a distribution invariant, never a preference."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ;
    logic:trigger gmeow:mediumCodec ;
    logic:triggerValue gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable ;
    logic:requires gmeow:mediumZstdLevel ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:Medium ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:GtsFrameProfileViolation ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:Medium using the mandated gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable must declare its gmeow:mediumZstdLevel — the mandated frame profile is the (transform, level) pair, and half a pair pins nothing." .

# The envelope's dictionary is exactly-one IFF its medium declares one. An
# unconditional min-1 restriction on gmeow:envelopeDictionary would make
# gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 — whose whole purpose is to be the named,
# explicitly dictionary-LESS medium — inexpressible as an envelope, so the
# obligation is GUARDED on the medium instead: an envelope written through the
# dictionary-declaring gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 must name the dictionary it was
# primed with, while an envelope over the baseline medium legitimately names
# none. The max-1 half stays an unconditional restriction (above), because a
# payload primed with two dictionaries is incoherent under every medium.
logic:MediumEnvelopeDictionaryConstraint
    a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium envelope-dictionary constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:MediumEnvelope whose gmeow:envelopeMedium is the dictionary-declaring gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 names a gmeow:envelopeDictionary. An undeclared dictionary is undiscoverable, so the payload is permanently undecodable even though its bytes are intact. It is deliberately GUARDED rather than unconditional: gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 declares an empty gmeow:mediumDictionary set, and under that medium naming NO dictionary is the selection, not an omission."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:MediumEnvelope ;
    logic:trigger gmeow:envelopeMedium ;
    logic:triggerValue gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 ;
    logic:requires gmeow:envelopeDictionary ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:MediumEnvelope ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:MediumEnvelope written through gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 must name the gmeow:envelopeDictionary its payload was primed with — an undeclared dictionary leaves intact bytes permanently undecodable." .

# The AUTHORED twin of the same conditional obligation, one level up: a
# registered rep assigned the dictionary-declaring medium must SELECT one of that
# medium's dictionaries. Without this the assignment would be total over media
# but partial over dictionaries, and a per-rep medium with no per-rep selection
# is exactly the encode-time guess the axis exists to remove.
logic:PayloadSchemaDictionaryConstraint
    a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Payload-schema dictionary constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:PayloadSchema whose gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium is the dictionary-declaring gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 names a gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary. Under gmeow:mediumSourcePerRep each registered schema selects its own dictionary from the medium's declared bound, so a rep with no selection would leave that choice to the encoder — the silent per-call decision the medium axis removes. A schema assigned the dictionary-less gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 is untouched: naming none IS its selection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:PayloadSchema ;
    logic:trigger gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium ;
    logic:triggerValue gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 ;
    logic:requires gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:PayloadSchema ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:PayloadSchema assigned gmeow:mediumProfileDistL12 must select a gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary from that medium's declared gmeow:mediumDictionary bound — a per-rep medium with no per-rep selection defers the choice to encode time." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Medium-axis declarative constraint axioms — authored ONCE in the CANONICAL   #
# logic: restriction vocabulary and PROJECTED to                              #
# generated/shapes/validation-shapes.ttl by derive_validation_shapes           #
# (Principle 17). The rdfs:/owl: spelling is the derived projection, never a   #
# hand-authored second source: an owl:Restriction written here would be        #
# ungrounded structural residue against this slice's projection-vocabulary     #
# ceiling, and the slice ships NO shapes.ttl.                                  #
#                                                                             #
# Two forms are used deliberately. A restriction qualified on owl:Thing is the #
# VACUOUS-QUALIFIER form the deriver degrades to plain sh:minCount/sh:maxCount #
# (and its owl:onDataRange twin degrades to sh:datatype + the same counts).    #
# A restriction qualified on a NAMED class keeps its count inside              #
# sh:qualifiedValueShape, and only earns a bare sh:class when a genuine        #
# universal backs it — here a closed-world-opted-in rdfs:range, declared by the#
# logic:ClosureEntry records below. rdfs:domain/range are open-world INFERENCE #
# axioms, so without an explicit opt-in the derive keeps their closed-world    #
# reading suppressed.                                                          #
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:envelopeDictionaryRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "envelope-dictionary range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:envelopeDictionary's rdfs:range gmeow:CompressionDictionary as a validation obligation: every dictionary an envelope names is a REGISTERED gmeow:CompressionDictionary, not merely inferable as one — an unregistered dictionary is gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary, a hard fail."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/envelopeDictionary" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary .

gmeow:envelopeSchemaRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "envelope-schema range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:envelopeSchema's rdfs:range gmeow:PayloadSchema as a validation obligation: every payload rep an envelope names is a REGISTERED gmeow:PayloadSchema — an unregistered rep is gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema, a hard fail rather than an unclassified blob."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/envelopeSchema" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema .

gmeow:mediumCorrespondenceRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "medium-correspondence range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:mediumCorrespondence's rdfs:range logic:Correspondence as a validation obligation: the losslessness judgment a medium points at is a declared logic:Correspondence, never an untyped node standing in for one — which is what keeps the round-trip claim a judged, dischargeable crossing instead of a flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mediumCorrespondence" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure .

gmeow:trainsOverCorpusRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "trains-over-corpus range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:trainsOverCorpus's rdfs:range gmeow:DictionaryCorpus as a validation obligation: the corpus a dictionary trains over is a declared gmeow:DictionaryCorpus, so the bundle-internal guarantee is stated somewhere a validator can reach."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/trainsOverCorpus" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure .

gmeow:payloadSchemaMediumRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "payload-schema medium range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium's rdfs:range gmeow:Medium as a validation obligation: the medium a registered payload rep is assigned is a DECLARED gmeow:Medium, never an untyped node standing in for one — an unresolvable assignment leaves the rep's round-trip law unstated, which is exactly the silent per-call decision the medium axis exists to remove."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/payloadSchemaMedium" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary .

gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionaryRangeClosure
    a logic:ClosureEntry ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "payload-schema dictionary range closure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The property-global closed-world authority reading gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary's rdfs:range gmeow:CompressionDictionary as a validation obligation: the dictionary a registered payload rep selects is a REGISTERED gmeow:CompressionDictionary — an unregistered one is gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary, a hard fail, never a fallback to a dictionary-less encode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    logic:closureKey "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/payloadSchemaDictionary" ;
    logic:closureValue logic:ClosedWorldClosure ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary .

# The medium-envelope contract. SIX fields are unconditionally exactly-one; the
# seventh — gmeow:envelopeDictionary — is exactly-one IFF the envelope's medium
# declares a dictionary at all. An unconditional min-1 here would make
# gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 INEXPRESSIBLE as an envelope: that medium
# declares an EMPTY gmeow:mediumDictionary set on purpose, and "no dictionary" is
# its selection, so an envelope over it legitimately names none. The conditional
# obligation is carried by logic:MediumEnvelopeDictionaryConstraint below, which
# is where a guarded requirement belongs; the max-1 restriction stays
# unconditional, because a payload primed with two dictionaries is incoherent
# under every medium. The two registry-resolved fields are qualified on their
# named class (backed by the closure entries above, so the derived shape carries
# sh:class); the rest use the vacuous owl:Thing qualifier, which the deriver
# degrades to plain counts.
gmeow:MediumEnvelope logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeDictionary ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeSchema ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:PayloadSchema ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeSchema ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:PayloadSchema ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:contentDigest ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:contentDigest ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeMedium ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeMedium ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopePayloadFrame ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopePayloadFrame ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeDigestStratum ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:envelopeDigestStratum ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:strataDigest ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:strataDigest ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] .

# A medium is exactly one codec, one resolution rule, and one judged crossing.
gmeow:Medium logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumCodec ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumCodec ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumSourceKind ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumSourceKind ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumCorrespondence ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Correspondence ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumCorrespondence ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Correspondence ] .

# A producer writes through exactly one medium, and governs at least one call
# site. "At least one" rather than "exactly one" is deliberate: a producer may
# legitimately span several files that write the SAME artifact through the SAME
# medium, while a row governing NO file classifies nothing.
gmeow:GtsProducer logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:producerMedium ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:producerMedium ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:producerCallSite ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] .

# The zstd level is declared on the medium, exactly once.
gmeow:ZstdDictMedium logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumZstdLevel ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:integer ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:mediumZstdLevel ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:integer ] .

# The AUTHORED dictionary contract. Deliberately NO digest / byte-length /
# Dictionary_ID obligation: those are build products, and requiring them on an
# authored individual would be an UNSATISFIABLE axiom rather than a strict one.
gmeow:CompressionDictionary logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryId ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryId ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryVersion ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryVersion ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryTargetLength ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryTargetLength ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryStrategy ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryStrategy ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:trainsOverCorpus ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:DictionaryCorpus ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:trainsOverCorpus ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:DictionaryCorpus ] .

# The GENERATED realization contract — where the measured fields ARE mandatory,
# because the build can always supply them.
gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:realizesDictionary ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:realizesDictionary ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryContentDigest ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryByteLength ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryByteLength ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:zstdDictionaryId ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:zstdDictionaryId ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryVersion ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:dictionaryVersion ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredDictionaryStrategy ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredDictionaryStrategy ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredDictionaryTargetLength ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredDictionaryTargetLength ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredCorpusSampleCount ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredCorpusSampleCount ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] .

# The DECLARED held-out split is exactly one modulus and one residue. Both are
# mandatory for the same reason: a split missing either coordinate does not
# partition anything, so a dictionary resolved under it would silently be trained
# on every member of its archive again.
gmeow:CorpusTrainingSplit logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:splitHeldOutStride ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:splitHeldOutStride ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:splitHeldOutOffset ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:splitHeldOutOffset ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] .

# The GENERATED dictionary-effect reading. Every field is mandatory and
# exactly-one, because every one of them is a build product the terminal can
# always supply and a reading missing any of them cannot be checked: the
# criterion is a COMPARISON, and a comparison with a missing operand is not a
# weaker claim, it is no claim.
gmeow:MediumDictionaryEffectMeasurement logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuresDictionary ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measuresDictionary ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementPopulation ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:MediumMeasurementPopulation ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementPopulation ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:MediumMeasurementPopulation ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementBytesOnDisk ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementBytesOnDisk ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementBytesOnDiskBaseline ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementBytesOnDiskBaseline ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementDictionaryInBandBytes ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementDictionaryInBandBytes ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementTwoPartCodeBytes ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementTwoPartCodeBytes ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementCorpusSampleCount ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementCorpusSampleCount ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementEvaluatedFrameCount ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:measurementEvaluatedFrameCount ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] .

# A registered payload schema carries exactly one wire label — the join key the
# carrier's representation constants are enumerated against — and exactly one
# assigned gmeow:Medium, which is what makes the rep-to-medium assignment TOTAL
# by construction rather than by inspection: every emittable rep already has a
# schema, so requiring the medium HERE means no payload can reach the wire with
# an undeclared one. The per-rep dictionary is at-most-one and CONDITIONAL (see
# logic:PayloadSchemaDictionaryConstraint): under the explicitly dictionary-less
# gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 its absence is the selection.
gmeow:PayloadSchema logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:payloadSchemaId ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:payloadSchemaId ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:string ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:payloadSchemaMedium ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:Medium ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] .

# =========================================================================== #
# Medium-axis procedural constraints — the cross-node conditions with no OWL   #
# antecedent, authored as canonical logic: constraints and lowered to          #
# sh:SPARQLConstraint node shapes. They are the SOLE authority for these       #
# checks; no hand-authored shape restates them.                                #
# =========================================================================== #

# A corpus with no selector declares nothing: its dictionary's training set
# would be undefined, so the bundle-internal guarantee could not be checked.
# Disjunctive requiredness has no OWL antecedent (it is "at least one of four
# DIFFERENT properties"), so it is a logic: constraint rather than a restriction.
logic:DictionaryCorpusSelectorConstraint
    a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "Dictionary-corpus selector constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:DictionaryCorpus declares at least one selector — a blob rep, a named graph, a path prefix, or a stage product. A corpus with no selector leaves its dictionary's training set undefined, so neither the reviewer nor the bundle-internal check has anything to read."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:DictionaryCorpus ;
    logic:anyOf gmeow:corpusSelectsBlobRep ,
        gmeow:corpusSelectsGraph ,
        gmeow:corpusSelectsPathPrefix ,
        gmeow:corpusSelectsStageProduct ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:DictionaryCorpus ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:DictionaryCorpus must declare at least one selector (gmeow:corpusSelectsBlobRep, gmeow:corpusSelectsGraph, gmeow:corpusSelectsPathPrefix, or gmeow:corpusSelectsStageProduct)." .

# A declared dict_id must resolve to a REGISTERED dictionary. Cross-node: the
# obligation is about the envelope's neighbour, not about the envelope's own
# cardinality, so it has no OWL antecedent.
logic:MediumDictionaryResolutionConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium dictionary-resolution constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every dictionary a gmeow:MediumEnvelope declares resolves to a registered gmeow:CompressionDictionary. HARD FAIL — an unresolvable dictionary makes the payload undecodable, and decoding it unprimed would yield corrupt output rather than degraded output, so there is no fallback."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:MediumEnvelope ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:MediumEnvelope's gmeow:envelopeDictionary must resolve to a registered gmeow:CompressionDictionary — an unknown dictionary is a hard failure, never a fallback to dictionary-less decode." ;
    logic:integrity logic:mdrForall .
logic:mdrForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:mdrImpl .
logic:mdrImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:mdrGuard ; logic:consequent logic:mdrNot .
logic:mdrGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:MediumEnvelope ] .
logic:mdrNot a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:mdrEx .
logic:mdrEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dict" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:mdrBody .
logic:mdrBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:mdrEdge , logic:mdrUnregistered .
logic:mdrEdge a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:envelopeDictionary ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "dict" ] .
logic:mdrUnregistered a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:mdrTyped .
logic:mdrTyped a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dict" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] .

# Every payload rep resolves to EXACTLY ONE declared medium. Combined with the
# exactly-one gmeow:envelopeMedium restriction above, this makes the rep-to-medium
# assignment a total FUNCTION: a schema two envelopes disagree about has no
# derivable medium, which is precisely the silent per-call decision the medium
# axis exists to remove.
logic:MediumSchemaMediumFunctionalityConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Payload-schema medium functionality constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: no two gmeow:MediumEnvelope records over the SAME gmeow:PayloadSchema may name different media. The rep-to-medium map is a function — 'which medium applies to this rep' must be derivable from the declaration, not decided per call."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:PayloadSchema ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema ;
    logic:message "A gmeow:PayloadSchema must resolve to exactly one declared gmeow:Medium — two envelopes over the same rep naming different media leave the rep's medium underivable." ;
    logic:integrity logic:msmForall .
logic:msmForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:msmImpl .
logic:msmImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:msmGuard ; logic:consequent logic:msmNot .
logic:msmGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:PayloadSchema ] .
logic:msmNot a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:msmEx .
logic:msmEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "envA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "envB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 2 ; logic:termVariable "mediumA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 3 ; logic:termVariable "mediumB" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:msmBody .
logic:msmBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:msmSchemaA , logic:msmSchemaB , logic:msmMediumA , logic:msmMediumB , logic:msmDistinct .
logic:msmSchemaA a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:envelopeSchema ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "envA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] .
logic:msmSchemaB a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:envelopeSchema ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "envB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] .
logic:msmMediumA a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:envelopeMedium ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "envA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "mediumA" ] .
logic:msmMediumB a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:envelopeMedium ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "envB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "mediumB" ] .
logic:msmDistinct a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termDistinct ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "mediumA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "mediumB" ] .

# One dictionary, ONE corpus identity. Cross-node: the obligation is about two
# realizations of the same definition agreeing, not about either one's own
# cardinality, so it has no OWL antecedent. It is the graph-side half of the
# corpus-drift refusal — the build's half re-derives every resolved corpus's digest
# and compares it against the committed sweep evidence — and both raise the same
# named failure, because both are "the recorded corpus is not the corpus at hand".
logic:MediumCorpusIdentityAgreementConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium corpus-identity agreement constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: no two gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization records of the SAME gmeow:CompressionDictionary may carry different gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest values. A dictionary's shipped bytes are a function of one corpus resolution, so two identities for one definition means at least one of them describes material those bytes did not come from — and the committed sweep evidence is compared against exactly that literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumCorpusDrift ;
    logic:message "Two gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization records of one gmeow:CompressionDictionary must agree on gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest — a dictionary whose evidence names two corpora has bytes that answer to neither." ;
    logic:integrity logic:mciForall .
logic:mciForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:mciImpl .
logic:mciImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:mciGuard ; logic:consequent logic:mciNot .
logic:mciGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:CompressionDictionary ] .
logic:mciNot a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:mciEx .
logic:mciEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "realA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "realB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 2 ; logic:termVariable "digestA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 3 ; logic:termVariable "digestB" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:mciBody .
logic:mciBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:mciRealizesA , logic:mciRealizesB , logic:mciDigestA , logic:mciDigestB , logic:mciDistinct .
logic:mciRealizesA a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:realizesDictionary ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "realA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] .
logic:mciRealizesB a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:realizesDictionary ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "realB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] .
logic:mciDigestA a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "realA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "digestA" ] .
logic:mciDigestB a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:measuredCorpusDigest ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "realB" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "digestB" ] .
logic:mciDistinct a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termDistinct ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "digestA" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "digestB" ] .

# Every EMITTED dictionary version is retained by its authored definition.
# Dropping a version orphans every artifact already primed with it — those bytes
# become undecodable, so retention is a data-preservation obligation, not tidiness.
logic:MediumDictionaryRetentionConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Medium dictionary-retention constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization's gmeow:dictionaryVersion is still declared by the gmeow:CompressionDictionary it gmeow:realizesDictionary. A version present in an emitted realization but absent from its authored definition has been RETIRED underneath shipped artifacts, and every payload primed with it is now undecodable."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization ;
    gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression ;
    logic:message "An emitted gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization's gmeow:dictionaryVersion must still be declared by the gmeow:CompressionDictionary it realizes — retiring a shipped version orphans every artifact primed with it." ;
    logic:integrity logic:mdtForall .
logic:mdtForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:mdtImpl .
logic:mdtImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:mdtGuard ; logic:consequent logic:mdtNot .
logic:mdtGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization ] .
logic:mdtNot a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:mdtEx .
logic:mdtEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "def" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "ver" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:mdtBody .
logic:mdtBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:mdtRealizes , logic:mdtEmitted , logic:mdtDropped .
logic:mdtRealizes a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:realizesDictionary ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "def" ] .
logic:mdtEmitted a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:dictionaryVersion ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "ver" ] .
logic:mdtDropped a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:mdtDeclared .
logic:mdtDeclared a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:dictionaryVersion ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "def" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "ver" ] .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects owl:FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.
#   logic:KeyAssertion — logic:keyProperty's value uniquely identifies a logic:keyClass instance.

gmeow:codecClassFunctionality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "codecClass is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:codecClass is functional: a gmeow:TransformCodec has exactly one capability class — the single kind of thing a reader must hold to reverse it, a library or a key, never both at once."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:codecClass ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:codecClass ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:codecClass names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:codecClass, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:codecClass and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:codecClass (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:codecClassFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:codecClass ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:gtsHeadIdFunctionality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "gtsHeadId is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:gtsHeadId is functional: a gmeow:GTSSegment has exactly one chain head — the single content-id of its last frame, written 'blake3:<hex>', which transitively commits to the segment's entire frame history. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:gtsHeadId ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:gtsHeadId ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:gtsHeadId names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:gtsHeadId, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:gtsHeadId and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:gtsHeadId (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:gtsHeadIdFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:gtsHeadId ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:gtsProfileFunctionality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/gts> ;
    rdfs:label "gtsProfile is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:gtsProfile is functional: a gmeow:GTSSegment declares exactly one profile — a single value-vocabulary individual naming its purpose and requirement set, while a multi-segment document's effective requirements are the derived union of its segments' profiles rather than a second value on one segment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:gtsProfile ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:gtsProfile ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:gtsProfile names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
